  "title": "Neural decoding of competitive decision-making in Rock-Paper-Scissors",
  "description": "This dataset contains 64-channel EEG recordings from 62 participants, organized into 31 pairs, who played a computerised version of the competitive Rock-Paper-Scissors game across 480 games. It was collected to study the neural correlates of competitive decision-making and to support decoding of choices and outcomes from brain activity. Each session lasted about one hour.",
  "methods_description": "Pairs of participants played 480 games of a computerised Rock-Paper-Scissors task while 64-channel EEG was recorded from both players. The experiment lasted approximately 1 hour.",
